453	The First Broken Bridge
454	Collect 6 Bridge Planks and fix the broken bridge to the east
455	It's been three months since the great wind stopped. The island sinks a fingernail's width every day.
456	When the east bridge broke, its planks scattered across the fields, and now the murklings are hauling them off for their nests.
457	Find me just six planks. A Mender like you can lay a bridge again.
458	Ho ho, the bridge is whole again! The road is open all the way to Pinwheel Hill.
459	Fluffling Trouble
460	Defeat 15 flufflings in the fields
461	Seen a fluffling yet? With the wind gone, they crawled up from under the clouds to eat what's left.
462	The more of them there are, the faster the island sinks. Could you teach fifteen of them a lesson?
463	Thank you. I can feel a little wind coming back. Here, take the ring I used to wear.
464	Pinwheel Hill
465	Defeat the Fluffling Chief on Pinwheel Hill
466	Ever since the pinwheel on the hilltop stopped, a huge fluffling has been sucking up all the wind there.
467	Defeat it and lay your hand on the Pinwheel Beacon. A little breath will return to the island.
468	Hear that? The pinwheel turning… first time in three months.
469	But the sky over Nest Isle doesn't look right. Someone says they saw the shadow of huge wings.
470	Musoe's Errand
471	Bring 3 Wind Whetstones
472	Want to learn enchanting? Murklings in the fields sometimes drop Wind Whetstones. Bring me three.
473	Weapons up to +6 and armor up to +4 never break. Past that it's luck. Fail, and it drops one step.
474	Good. Here's your pay: a Blessed Whetstone. Nothing's lost if it fails, and sometimes it jumps two steps at once.
475	The Bridge to Reed Marsh
476	Defeat Nestkeepers, collect 3 Nest Shells, and fix the bridge east of the hill
477	East of Pinwheel Hill there was a bridge to Reed Marsh. That one broke too.
478	Nestkeeper shells are hard as stone, perfect for bridge supports. Gather three and lay the bridge again.
479	Past the marsh lies Nest Isle, where that great winged shadow landed.
480	The road to Reed Marsh is open! Nest Isle is at the far end of that marsh… be careful, Mender.
481	Clearing Reed Marsh
482	Defeat 20 murklings in Reed Marsh
483	Reed Marsh is crawling with mud flufflings and pods. Pods spit mud from afar, so get up close and deal with them.
484	Thin them out by twenty or so and the marsh wind will clear.
485	The marsh is starting to smell of wind. Thank you, take this earring I treasured.
486	The Great Heron of Nest Isle
487	Defeat the Great Heron of Nest Isle and touch Nest Isle's Pinwheel Beacon
488	The Great Heron of Nest Isle has hidden all the island's wind under its wings. That's why Dandelion Isle is sinking.
489	It stabs with its beak, shoves with its wings, and calls its chicks. When enraged, it rains feathers from the sky.
490	Careful not to get pushed off the edge. Defeat it and Dandelion Isle will breathe again.
491	…Hear that? Wind rising from beneath the island. Dandelion Isle has stopped sinking!
492	All thanks to you, Mender. But rumor says the reason the great wind stopped lies further on, in the Rusty Windmill Isles.
493	A Windway has opened at the Pinwheel Beacon. Cross over when you're ready.
494	The great wind stopped.
495	The bridges between the islands broke, and the islands are slowly sinking into the sea of clouds.
496	You drifted down onto Dandelion Isle on a single rag sail — a Mender, who joins broken paths again.
